43](/home/joe/code/mathlib4/DarkTower/BaldwinDesign.lean:143).\n\nThe TSV output retains only population means and a few best scalars at [baldwin_selection.clj:265](/home/joe/code/mmca-clj/scripts/baldwin_selection.clj:265). It discards:\n\n- Complete genomes.\n- Parent and donor identities.\n- Mutation/HGT transitions.\n- Best genome’s raw reach.\n- Raw band score separate from cost-adjusted fitness.\n- Held-rule endpoint evaluations.\n\nEven if assimilation occurred, the run could not produce the Lean certificate.\n\n4. The calibration invariant still fails\n\nThe selection score uses the 8–22 thresholds derived from periodic ECA dynamics, but the experiment evolves phenotypes with zero boundaries:\n\n- Zero-boundary dynamics: [core.clj:65](/home/joe/code/mmca-clj/src/mmca/core.clj:65)\n- Periodic calibration: [regime_placement.clj:62](/home/joe/code/mmca-clj/scripts/regime_placement.clj:62)\n\nUnder zero boundaries, rule 30 measures about 18.4—inside the supposed complex band. Thus the score can classify a calibration-chaotic endpoint as successful. Until calibration and construction dynamics agree, “high function” is not well-defined.\n\n5. The new preflight is unsound\n\nThe current uncommitted preflight begins at [baldwin_selection.clj:201](/home/joe/code/mmca-clj/scripts/baldwin_selection.clj:201).\n\nConcrete counterexamples:\n\n- Its I3 check only confirms that keys exist. I supplied a child whose `field` came from one parent and `hold` from the other; the check returned `true`, although linkage was false.\n- Its I4 check covers only gamma and update probability, omitting `field`, `mask`, and `hold`.\n- Its I6 check accepts any profile with two distinct scores. The known forbidden profile `[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, positive]` passes.\n- It omits I1, I5, I7, I8, I9, and I10.\n- `--skip-preflight` bypasses the gate entirely, contrary to the workspace rule against routing around invariants.\n- It prints “all applicable invariants pass” despite checking only four, 